Add a "claude" widget to MacShell's bar: the Claude logo plus the % used of the plan's 5-hour session, coloured by level (green < 50%, yellow < 75%, orange < 90%, red from there on). A click opens a popover with the account email, the 5-hour and 7-day limits (coloured meter, % used, reset time) and today's tokens per model (a share bar and a dot in each model family's colour; input, output, cache write / read).

Data comes from <repo>/macshell/claude-usage.py, polled every 60 s (and when the popover opens) while the widget is on, the bar is shown and Game Mode is off:
  - plan limits and account email: ~/.cache/claude-usage.json, written by <repo>/claude/statusline.sh, which must be
    Claude Code's status line ("statusLine": {"type": "command", "command": "~/Documents/danie_dotfiles/claude/statusline.sh"}
    in ~/.claude/settings.json). They only refresh while a Claude Code session is running.
  - tokens today: ~/.claude/projects/**/*.jsonl, deduplicated by (message.id, requestId).
The logo is <repo>/macshell/claude-logo.svg. Both paths are hardcoded under ~/Documents/danie_dotfiles/macshell (claudeDir in MacBar.qml).

Apply (after ram-widget.patch; a MacShell update may overwrite MacBar.qml, so re-apply afterwards):
  cd ~/.local/share/macshell/MacShell && patch -p1 < <repo>/macshell/claude-widget.patch
Then enable it by adding "claude" to "barWidgets" in ~/.config/macbar/settings.json.
settings.json is only read at load, and patching MacBar.qml does not trigger Quickshell's hot reload, so restart MacShell:
  qs kill -p ~/.local/share/macshell/MacShell; uwsm-app -t service -- sh ~/.local/share/macshell/start

